index 0000000..aab7729
--- /dev/null
+++ b/BUILD-WINDOWS.md
@@ -0,0 +1,92 @@
+# Eclipse Pro — Windows 11 Build Guide
+
+Eclipse Pro ka saara UI code **pure Python** me hai — ise compile karne ki
+zaroorat nahi. Lekin video engine (**libopenshot**, C++) Windows par build
+karna padta hai. Ye guide wahi process deta hai.
+
+## Step 1 — Python + Qt
+
+1. [python.org](https://www.python.org/downloads/) se **Python 3.11+** install
+   karo (install ke time "Add python.exe to PATH" tick karna).
+2. Is folder me terminal kholo aur chalao:
+
+```
+pip install -r requirements.txt
+```
+
+## Step 2 — libopenshot build karo (sabse bhari step)
+
+Official docs ke hisaab se Windows par libopenshot **MSYS2 + MinGW** se
+build hota hai (Visual Studio se seedha nahi):
+
+- https://github.com/OpenShot/libopenshot/wiki/Windows-Build-Instructions
+- https://github.com/openshot/libopenshot/blob/HEAD/doc/INSTALL-WINDOWS.md
+
+Summary:
+
+```
+# MSYS2 MinGW 64-bit terminal me:
+cd /c/path/to/libopenshot-audio
+mkdir build && cd build
+cmake -G "MinGW Makefiles" ..
+mingw32-make
+mingw32-make install
+
+cd /c/path/to/libopenshot
+mkdir build && cd build
+cmake -G "MinGW Makefiles" -DUSE_QT6=ON ..
+mingw32-make
+mingw32-make install
+```
+
+Build ke baad verify karo:
+
+```
+python -c "import openshot; print(openshot.__file__)"
+```
+
+Agar `import openshot` chal gaya, engine ready hai.
+
+> Note: `make install` Python bindings (`_openshot.pyd` + `openshot.py`)
+> ko Python ke site-packages me daal deta hai. Agar install skip kiya hai
+> to `run-eclipse.bat` me `PYTHONPATH` wali line uncomment karke build
+> folder ka `bindings/python` path set karo.
+
+## Step 3 — Eclipse Pro chalao
+
+```
+run-eclipse.bat
+```
+
+ya seedha:
+
+```
+python src\launch.py
+```
+
+Pehli baar me **Eclipse (Premiere Pro style) dark theme** aur naya dock
+layout (Project | Program | Effect Controls + full-width Timeline) dikhega.
+
+## Step 4 — EclipsePro.exe banao (optional)
+
+Jab upar wala run stable ho jaye, tab exe freeze karo. OpenShot ke
+official Windows installer bhi **cx_Freeze** se bante hain:
+
+```
+pip install cx_Freeze
+cxfreeze src\launch.py --target-dir dist\EclipsePro --target-name EclipsePro.exe
+```
+
+> Imaandar note: freeze karne par Qt ke DLLs, libopenshot ke DLLs aur
+> FFmpeg ko saath bundle karna padta hai. Pehli baar me kuch missing-DLL
+> errors aana normal hai — jis DLL ki complaint aaye, use `dist\EclipsePro`
+> me copy karo jab tak exe khul na jaye. Ye trial-and-error wala hissa
+> tumhari machine par hi hoga, isliye is step ki exact file-list yahan
+> pehle se nahi likhi ja sakti.
+
+## Shortcut — overlay trick (advanced)
+
+Ek maintainer ke hisaab se Windows par aksar sirf 4 files badalni padti
+hain: official OpenShot install karo, fir apni built DLLs/`_openshot.pyd`
+ko install folder ke upar copy kar do. Ye tez hai lekin version-sensitive
+hai — recommended sirf tab jab Step 2 me atak jao.
